course: dictionary
lesson: 10699
title: Unseen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unseen means not seen or not noticed by anyone. The prefix un- means "not", so unseen is "not seen". «Most of the Earth's volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor» tells you the activity is real, but nobody is there to watch it.
explain: Unseen can also mean something you cannot see but that is still there. Germs and air are unseen, but they are real. An unseen danger is one you cannot spot until it is too late.
explain: In school, an unseen passage or unseen poem is one you read for the first time in a test. You cannot have practised it, so you must use context clues, reading the words around each new word to work out what it means.
fact: Unseen means not seen or not noticed by anyone.
fact: The prefix un- means "not", so unseen means "not seen".
fact: «Unseen» can also describe something real that you cannot see, such as germs or air.
fact: In school, an unseen passage is a text you read for the first time in a test.
fact: «Sight unseen» means choosing or buying something without looking at it first.
exercise: «Most volcanic activity happens unseen on the ocean floor.» What does unseen mean here? | Very loud and bright | Left over from long ago | *Not seen by anyone | Easy to see from the land
exercise: In school, what is an unseen passage? | *A text you have not looked at before | A passage with pictures | A passage you have read many times before | A passage that is very short
exercise: Mia says germs are unseen, but they are still real. What does unseen tell you about germs? | They are always big | *They cannot be seen with the eye | They are dangerous only at night | They are made of wood
test: «At Newcastle University, people paid more into an honesty box when a picture of eyes hung above it.» Find and copy the word that means not noticed by anyone. | picture | *we | people | honesty
test: «We are tempted most when we feel unseen.» Which word is closest in meaning to unseen? | Hungry | Busy | Loud | *Hidden from notice
exam: Ravi reads «a quiet kindness nobody knows about». What does unseen mean if the kindness goes unseen? | Very large | Shared with the whole class | Not noticed by anyone | *Not seen or known by anyone
